    "tol-history-math": {
      "schema": "sunny.tol-history-mathematical-reconstruction.v1",
      "created_utc": "2026-10-31T21:40:13.961720+00:00",
      "selection_receipt": "docs/evidence/mandate-tol-unit-superjev.json",
      "solver_receipt": "docs/evidence/mandate-tol-wolfram.json",
      "unit_status": "bounded_conditional_derivation_executed; not a complete TOL type system or global orientation",
      "source_spans": [
        {
          "id": "primitive_scalar_operations",
          "document_id": "266d779908f5dadee900884fae6c6d6d69e07cf7372dd61f4c686319b3436e6e",
          "source_id": "6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9",
          "source_path": "C:\\Users\\Brend\\Documents\\ChatGPT\\SUN\\data\\raw\\archive\\SUN_Universal_Archive\\Library\\RELATED_LINEAGES\\TOL_COMPLETE_WORK_ARCHIVE_2026-09-29 (1).md",
          "source_sha256": "1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065",
          "source_role": "historical_recovered_research_archive",
          "extracted_document_lines": [
            198,
            252
          ],
          "document_char_start": 5839,
          "document_char_end": 6563,
          "exact_quote": "## 5. Primitive transformations\n\nFor a carrier/reference state \\(C\\), the recovered operators were:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nR(C)=\\frac23C\n}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nL(C)=\\frac34C\n}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nO(C)=\\frac12C\n}\n\\]\n\nwith the exact closure identity:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nR\\circ L=L\\circ R=O\n}\n\\]\n\nbecause:\n\n\\[\n\\frac23\\cdot\\frac34=\\frac12.\n\\]\n\nThe recursion policy was written:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nC_n\n\\xrightarrow{R,L}\n\\{R(C_n),L(C_n)\\}\n\\xrightarrow{\\text{closure}}\nC_{n+1}\n}\n\\]\n\nand in simplified form:\n\n\\[\nC_{n+1}=O(C_n).\n\\]\n\nAn important later correction was retained: this is a **compositional/transformation identity**, not automatically an acoustic claim that simultaneously sounding the branches physically produces the lower octave as a spectral component.",
          "quote_sha256": "ed36007064aacf34b0808c608859bda271011b50567a2ae865abeea81a0b84e6",
          "locator_boundary": "Lines and offsets address the stored extracted document; source file bytes are separately hash-verified."
        },
        {
          "id": "history_and_observable_projection",
          "document_id": "266d779908f5dadee900884fae6c6d6d69e07cf7372dd61f4c686319b3436e6e",
          "source_id": "6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9",
          "source_path": "C:\\Users\\Brend\\Documents\\ChatGPT\\SUN\\data\\raw\\archive\\SUN_Universal_Archive\\Library\\RELATED_LINEAGES\\TOL_COMPLETE_WORK_ARCHIVE_2026-09-29 (1).md",
          "source_sha256": "1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065",
          "source_role": "historical_recovered_research_archive",
          "extracted_document_lines": [
            258,
            323
          ],
          "document_char_start": 6604,
          "document_char_end": 7731,
          "exact_quote": "## 6. Internal history versus observable value\n\nOne of the strongest pieces of the TOL formalization was the explicit refusal to collapse different causal histories merely because their outputs coincide.\n\nLet the history-bearing state space be:\n\n\\[\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal C}=(\\mathcal C,h).\n\\]\n\nThen it is permitted that:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\widetilde L\\widetilde R(x)\n\\neq\n\\widetilde R\\widetilde L(x)\n}\n\\]\n\ninternally.\n\nAn observation/projection map:\n\n\\[\nq:\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal C}\n\\rightarrow\n\\mathcal C_{\\mathrm{observable}}\n\\]\n\ncan nevertheless satisfy:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nq(\\widetilde L\\widetilde R(x))\n=\nq(\\widetilde R\\widetilde L(x))\n=\nq(\\widetilde O(x))\n}\n\\]\n\nThis was called **confluence modulo the observable quotient**.\n\nEquivalently, define:\n\n\\[\nx\\sim_q y\n\\iff\nq(x)=q(y).\n\\]\n\nThen different histories can be observationally equivalent without becoming the same derivation.\n\nCore rule:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\text{equivalent observation}\n\\not\\Rightarrow\n\\text{identical derivation}\n}\n\\]\n\nThis became a provenance-preservation principle and later aligns directly with SUN V2's rule that equal relational effect does not imply equal path/address.",
          "quote_sha256": "31a708145253eafb9e837e7197a0db8c89590b2e401dc7bf7a2ada2253d98da6",
          "locator_boundary": "Lines and offsets address the stored extracted document; source file bytes are separately hash-verified."
        },
        {
          "id": "prime_coordinates_and_evaluation",
          "document_id": "266d779908f5dadee900884fae6c6d6d69e07cf7372dd61f4c686319b3436e6e",
          "source_id": "6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9",
          "source_path": "C:\\Users\\Brend\\Documents\\ChatGPT\\SUN\\data\\raw\\archive\\SUN_Universal_Archive\\Library\\RELATED_LINEAGES\\TOL_COMPLETE_WORK_ARCHIVE_2026-09-29 (1).md",
          "source_sha256": "1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065",
          "source_role": "historical_recovered_research_archive",
