          "document_char_start": 13190,
          "document_char_end": 14367,
          "exact_quote": "## 13. 3-limit multiplicative group\n\nThe most mature recovered algebraization defined:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\mathcal H_3\n=\n\\{2^a3^b:a,b\\in\\mathbb Z\\}\n}\n\\]\n\nas a 3-limit multiplicative group.\n\nUnder the prime-exponent coordinate map:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\nu_{2,3}(2^a3^b)=(a,b)\n}\n\\]\n\nmultiplication becomes vector addition.\n\nThe primitive operators map to:\n\n\\[\nR=\\frac23\n\\mapsto\n(1,-1)\n\\]\n\n\\[\nL=\\frac34\n\\mapsto\n(-2,1)\n\\]\n\n\\[\nO=\\frac12\n\\mapsto\n(-1,0).\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\nu(R)+\\nu(L)\n=\n(1,-1)+(-2,1)\n=\n(-1,0)\n=\n\\nu(O)\n}\n\\]\n\nThis gives an additive coordinate representation of the harmonic closure identity.\n\n## 14. Unevaluated versus evaluated harmonic spaces\n\nTo preserve operation order/history, the harmonic IR was split:\n\n\\[\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n\\mathcal H.\n\\]\n\nAn evaluation quotient:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nq_H=\\operatorname{eval}:\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\rightarrow\n\\mathcal H\n}\n\\]\n\npermits:\n\n\\[\nRL\\neq LR\n\\quad\\text{in }\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\]\n\nwhile:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\operatorname{eval}(RL)\n=\n\\operatorname{eval}(LR)\n=\n\\operatorname{eval}(O)\n=\n\\frac12\n}\n\\]\n\nin the evaluated harmonic space.\n\nThis is the harmonic-specific version of history-aware projected confluence.",
          "quote_sha256": "ae7dd3e5c6c5e93b3c2374e1ba59c12f8a075e33c4d39b51e38c07a900527b72",
          "locator_boundary": "Lines and offsets address the stored extracted document; source file bytes are separately hash-verified."
        },
        {
          "id": "faithfulness_protected_distinctions",
          "document_id": "266d779908f5dadee900884fae6c6d6d69e07cf7372dd61f4c686319b3436e6e",
          "source_id": "6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9",
          "source_path": "C:\\Users\\Brend\\Documents\\ChatGPT\\SUN\\data\\raw\\archive\\SUN_Universal_Archive\\Library\\RELATED_LINEAGES\\TOL_COMPLETE_WORK_ARCHIVE_2026-09-29 (1).md",
          "source_sha256": "1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065",
          "source_role": "historical_recovered_research_archive",
          "extracted_document_lines": [
            888,
            927
          ],
          "document_char_start": 16234,
          "document_char_end": 16840,
          "exact_quote": "## 17. What a valid domain mapping must preserve\n\nA domain realization:\n\n\\[\n\\rho_D:\n\\mathcal G\n\\rightarrow\n\\mathcal S_D\n\\]\n\nis not considered faithful merely because objects can be named correspondingly.\n\nThe mature criterion requires preservation of declared:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\{\n\\text{types},\n\\text{composition},\n\\text{equivalences},\n\\text{protected distinctions},\n\\text{history constraints}\n\\}\n}\n\\]\n\nand earlier versions expressed the test as:\n\n\\[\n\\rho_\\tau(RL(x))\n\\sim\n\\rho_\\tau(O(x)).\n\\]\n\nThe broader methodological rule was:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\text{align operators and relations, not merely entities or labels.}",
          "quote_sha256": "17816e65ea35e8b451e279ab6d86afff2ca4be2013f553e3b6b70515812651b1",
          "locator_boundary": "Lines and offsets address the stored extracted document; source file bytes are separately hash-verified."
        },
        {
          "id": "registered_partial_adapter",
          "document_id": "266d779908f5dadee900884fae6c6d6d69e07cf7372dd61f4c686319b3436e6e",
          "source_id": "6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9",
          "source_path": "C:\\Users\\Brend\\Documents\\ChatGPT\\SUN\\data\\raw\\archive\\SUN_Universal_Archive\\Library\\RELATED_LINEAGES\\TOL_COMPLETE_WORK_ARCHIVE_2026-09-29 (1).md",
          "source_sha256": "1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065",
          "source_role": "historical_recovered_research_archive",
          "extracted_document_lines": [
            1238,
            1321
          ],
          "document_char_start": 21157,
          "document_char_end": 22453,
          "exact_quote": "## 22. SUN V2 makes TOL's role explicit\n\nSUN V2 later imposed a much cleaner boundary around TOL.\n\nTOL remains **external to SUN's music-native derivation**.\n\nIts responsibility is to preserve:\n\n- native address;\n- path;\n- provenance;\n- relation type;\n- unitization;\n- class;\n- register;\n- source dependence;\n\nwhile enabling a registered relational projection into SUN.\n\nThe later formal expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\mathfrak N_v\n\\xrightarrow{A_v}\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal T}_v\n\\xrightarrow{P_\\Sigma}\nX_{\\rm SUN}\n}\n\\]\n\nFor an external/native system \\(v\\):\n\n\\[\nT_v:X_v\\rightarrow X_v\n\\]\n\nis its native transition law, while:\n\n\\[\nA_v:X_v\\rightharpoonup X_{\\rm SUN}\n\\]\n\nis the registered adapter.\n\nThe desired structural condition is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nA_v\\circ T_v\n=\nT_{\\rm SUN}\\circ A_v\n}\n\\]\n\nwhere established.\n\nIf \\(A_v\\) is non-invertible, this is semiconjugacy-like.\n\nIf invertible on the relevant region:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nT_{\\rm SUN}\n=\nA_vT_vA_v^{-1}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThe critical authority boundary is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\text{TOL helps test/preserve/translate relational dynamics;}\n}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\text{TOL does NOT generate }T_{\\rm SUN}.\n}\n\\]\n\nSUN must derive its native transition grammar independently from music. TOL may then determine whether another native system preserves the same dynamics under a lawful adapter.",
          "quote_sha256": "aeeaaf53c51f883e2c3a869cf0fcc141cb7b38a0a3bb271f2a5427a32cc2f36a",
          "locator_boundary": "Lines and offsets address the stored extracted document; source file bytes are separately hash-verified."
        },
        {
          "id": "unfinished_domains_and_type_system",
          "document_id": "266d779908f5dadee900884fae6c6d6d69e07cf7372dd61f4c686319b3436e6e",
          "source_id": "6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9",
          "source_path": "C:\\Users\\Brend\\Documents\\ChatGPT\\SUN\\data\\raw\\archive\\SUN_Universal_Archive\\Library\\RELATED_LINEAGES\\TOL_COMPLETE_WORK_ARCHIVE_2026-09-29 (1).md",
          "source_sha256": "1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065",
          "source_role": "historical_recovered_research_archive",
          "extracted_document_lines": [
            1455,
            1509
          ],
          "document_char_start": 26254,
          "document_char_end": 28433,
          "exact_quote": "# PART XX — WHAT WAS NOT FINISHED\n\n## 26. Unfinished formal work\n\nDespite substantial algebraization, the recovered archive does **not** establish a final locked standalone \"TOL Algebra v1.0\".\n\nOutstanding work includes:\n\n### A. Complete type system\n\nThe role vocabulary exists, but a complete formal type judgment system was not recovered, e.g.:\n\n\\[\n\\Gamma\\vdash f:A\\rightarrow B.\n\\]\n\n### B. Full domain/codomain specification\n\nEvery primitive and composite operator still needs explicit legal domains, codomains, partiality rules, and failure semantics.\n\n### C. Identity and associativity laws\n\nThe archive contains composition semantics but not a complete presentation proving all category/algebra axioms.\n\n### D. Closure theorem\n\nThe system still needs a proof specifying exactly under what operator vocabulary it is closed.\n\n### E. Complete address algebra\n\nTOL became an address/topology system, but the address transformations themselves were not fully axiomatized.\n\n### F. Unitization/class algebra\n\nLater SUN V2 introduces class, unitization, register, and address transitions more cleanly than the original TOL work. These need to be integrated without allowing TOL to manufacture SUN's native invariant.\n\n### G. Residual metric calibration\n\n\\(\\varepsilon\\) is defined structurally, and \\(\\|\\varepsilon\\|_w\\) was proposed, but the weights and comparison metric were not locked.\n\n### H. Faithfulness criteria\n\nThe preservation set is known conceptually, but exact mathematical conditions for faithful/partial/invalid realization remain to be formalized.\n\n### I. Boundary semantics\n\nMalkhut/boundary quotient is a strong candidate model, not a universally proved property of every Tree representation.\n\n### J. Historical versus structural evidence ledger\n\nThe project explicitly distinguishes historical descent from independent structural recurrence, but this distinction still needs a formal evidence schema if TOL becomes executable.\n\n### K. Standalone canonical specification\n\nMost importantly: the work evolved through several documents. It was never recovered as one frozen canonical TOL specification with versioning, axioms, proofs, test vectors, and lock status.",
          "quote_sha256": "f4c51e09d74926d74349e08c1c02db0b7dcd9147f21ff7b2c2ff1204b4990449",
          "locator_boundary": "Lines and offsets address the stored extracted document; source file bytes are separately hash-verified."
        }
      ],
