          "statement": "Positive prime-monomial normal form is faithful.",
          "assumptions": "Finite products of positive prime bases with rational exponents; no sums and no complex branch choices.",
          "argument": "If two products are equal, divide and raise to a common positive multiple N of every exponent denominator. Moving negative powers to the other side gives equality of positive integers with prime factorizations. Unique prime factorization forces every N*(alpha_p-beta_p)=0, hence alpha_p=beta_p. Conversely identical exponents give identical positive products.",
